thentication  scheme.   It does not use a Kerberos 5 exchange be‐
tween client and server, but rather  authenticates  the  password
provided by the client against the Kerberos KDC.  Therefore, care
should be taken to only use this module over a secure session se‐
cure  TTY, encrypted session, etc.  otherwise the user’s Kerberos
5 password could be compromised.
